WEBVTT

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.726
that's right, right?

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.643
Let me tell you about some of the costs

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:35.684
when we fail to tap
into our students' potential.

00:03:35.708 --> 00:03:38.643
A McKinsey study showed that if in 1998

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:41.893
we could've closed our long-standing
student achievement gaps

00:03:41.917 --> 00:03:44.184
between students
of different ethnic backgrounds

00:03:44.208 --> 00:03:46.768
or students of different income levels,

00:03:46.792 --> 00:03:49.518
by 2008, our GDP --

00:03:49.542 --> 00:03:51.351
our untapped economic gains --

00:03:51.375 --> 00:03:54.893
could have gone up
by more than 500 billion dollars.

00:03:54.917 --> 00:03:57.434
Those same gaps in 2008,

00:03:57.458 --> 00:04:01.643
between our students here in the US
and those across the world,